    "description": "Keytruda (pembrolizumab) is a PD-1 immune checkpoint inhibitor developed by Merck. It blocks the interaction between PD-1 and its ligands PD-L1/PD-L2, restoring T-cell mediated anti-tumor immune activity. It is approved across a broad range of solid tumor and hematologic indications.",
    "mechanism": "PD-1 immune checkpoint inhibitor — blocks PD-1 receptor interaction with PD-L1/PD-L2, restoring T-cell anti-tumor activity.",
    "target": "PD-1 (Programmed Death Receptor-1)"
  },

